# Keep the build context small. Anything Docker doesn't need to see during
# `docker build` should be listed here — it speeds up the initial context
# upload and prevents host-side build junk from invalidating cache layers.

# Node / Vite
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr

# Rust / Tauri build output
src-tauri/target
src-tauri/gen
src-tauri/.cargo

# Docker output volume from previous runs
dist-linux

# Git + CI metadata (the Rust/Node builds don't read these)
.git
.github

# Editor / OS junk
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Claude Code workspace state
.claude
CLAUDE.md

# Secrets — belt-and-braces; these should never be in the repo, but make
# sure they can't leak into a build context either.
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
loach.key
loach.key.pub
.tauri

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
